  "step": [
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1,
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "So, you've decided it's time for new kitchen cabinets, or maybe you're just updating the look of your kitchen. Removing the old ones is a big first step! It’s not just about unscrewing them from the wall; there's a bit more to it if you want to avoid headaches later on. First off, you'll need to clear everything out of your kitchen. I mean everything — dishes, appliances, decor. Then, it's super important to turn off any water and power connected to the cabinets, especially if you have a sink or under-cabinet lighting. Next, you’ll take off the doors and drawers and remove all the hardware. After that, carefully cut any caulk or trim that's holding the cabinets to the wall or ceiling. Once those are clear, you can start unscrewing the cabinets from the wall. Don't forget that base cabinets usually come out after the countertops and plumbing connections are handled. Getting this right sets you up for a smooth renovation. If you're feeling overwhelmed or unsure about any part of this, especially with plumbing or electrical, it's smart to chat with a professional. HH Remodeling LLC is here to help you through the process, ensuring everything is done safely and efficiently."
    }
  ],
